1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.ria1914.info/index.php/%D0%9C%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B2_%D0%9B%D0%B5%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BD_%D0%9F%D0%B5%D1%82%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%87 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Prince Levan Mellkov de Somhetie, member of the former ruling family of the principality of Georgia, Russia, will be held at Northam Chapel, Cedar Hill, at 3 p.m. today. Burial will be in Cedar Hill Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Levan, who died In New York last Thursday night was the husband of Rosalie Hooker Welling Dixon, daughter of Mrs. Mary Hooker of the Heubeln Hotel and the late Edward W. Hooker, once mayor, of Hartford.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the World War, the prince was captain of the Chevalier Guard Regiment of the Russian Imperial Guard. He became later aide-de-camp to the commander-in-chief of the Russian armies on the northern front. Following the outbreak
2 CONC  of the Russian Revolution, he was made assistant chief of staff of the Georgian armies in Batum. He served his country both in a military capacity and as a statesman.
2 CONT
2 CONT [CLIPPED FROM Hartford Courant, Hartford, Connecticut, 30 Jan 1928, Mon • Page 4]
